# Chain 2: Evidence-Aware Verification Pipeline

This plan outlines the integration of the Gemini 3.6 Flash Evidence Engine (Chain 2) into the existing FakeCheckPro platform. The design is purely additive and strictly preserves the existing Chain 1 ML pipeline, database schema, and UI structure.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> This plan introduces the `google-genai` dependency for the backend. Please confirm this is acceptable. 
> The Gemini API key will need to be provided in the `.env` file as `GEMINI_API_KEY`. 

## Proposed Changes

### Backend: Configuration & Dependencies
- **[MODIFY]** [`backend/requirements.txt`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/requirements.txt): Add `google-genai` for the current Gemini API SDK.
- **[MODIFY]** [`backend/.env.example`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/.env.example) and [`backend/.env`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/.env): Add `GEMINI_API_KEY`.

### Backend: Database & Schemas
- **[MODIFY]** [`backend/app/database/history_models.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/database/history_models.py): Add new additive SQLAlchemy models: `EvidenceVerification`, `VerificationClaim`, and `VerificationSource`. These will link to `PredictionHistory` via a `prediction_id` foreign key.
- **[NEW]** [`backend/app/schemas/evidence.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/schemas/evidence.py): Define Pydantic models for `EvidenceRequest`, `EvidenceResult`, `Claim`, and `Source` to enforce the strict JSON structure expected from Gemini.

### Backend: Services
- **[NEW]** [`backend/app/services/gemini_evidence_service.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/services/gemini_evidence_service.py): Implement the `GeminiEvidenceService` class. This will:
  - Initialize the `google-genai` client using the environment variable.
  - Formulate the system instructions according to the evidence rules (ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE IS NOT EVIDENCE OF FALSITY, Source Tiers, etc.).
  - Call `gemini-3.6-flash` with the Google Search tool enabled.
  - Enforce the structured JSON output.
- **[NEW]** [`backend/app/services/evidence_service.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/services/evidence_service.py): Act as a coordinator to call `GeminiEvidenceService` and persist the resulting data to the new database models.

### Backend: API Routes
- **[NEW]** [`backend/app/api/routes/evidence.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/api/routes/evidence.py): Create `POST /api/evidence/analyze`. It will accept the conceptual input (`article_text`, `ml_prediction`, `ml_confidence`, `source_url`, `history_id`) to maintain decoupling from Chain 1.
- **[MODIFY]** [`backend/app/main.py`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/backend/app/main.py): Include the new `evidence.py` router.

### Frontend: Services & UI
- **[MODIFY]** [`frontend/src/services/api.js`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/frontend/src/services/api.js): Add `analyzeEvidence(data)` function to call the new endpoint.
- **[NEW]** [`frontend/src/components/analyzer/EvidenceVerification.jsx`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/frontend/src/components/analyzer/EvidenceVerification.jsx): A new component to display the Evidence Score, Verification Status, Claims Analysis, and Evidence Summary.
- **[MODIFY]** [`frontend/src/pages/Analyze.jsx`](file:///d:/FakeCheckPro/frontend/src/pages/Analyze.jsx): Integrate the Chain 2 call. Once Chain 1 succeeds, asynchronously trigger Chain 2 and display a loading state for the Evidence Section. Once Chain 2 resolves, render `EvidenceVerification` alongside `PredictionCard`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create tests in `backend/test_evidence.py` or run manual tests simulating various scenarios (fake viral claim, true government announcement, no external corroboration) directly against the `/api/evidence/analyze` endpoint.

### Manual Verification
- Start the API and frontend.
- Submit a well-known fake news article and verify Chain 1 catches it and Chain 2 classifies it as `CONTRADICTED` or `LIKELY_MISLEADING` with sources.
- Submit a real recent news article and verify Chain 2 classifies it as `SUPPORTED` or `LIKELY_CREDIBLE`.
- Simulate a Google Search failure or API key absence to verify it falls back to `UNVERIFIED` without crashing Chain 1.
